cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CVE-2026-45362: Plaintext SIP Credentials in Switchvox Backups"
message: "If you use this research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Overholser
    given-names: Michael
    alias: wb6vpm

url: https://github.com/wb6vpm/switchvox-svb-plaintext-sip-credentials
repository-code: https://github.com/wb6vpm/switchvox-svb-plaintext-sip-credentials

abstract: >
  Technical analysis and incident documentation for CVE-2026-45362.
  Sangoma Switchvox On-Premise releases before 8.4 could store configured live
  SIP provider credentials in plaintext within .svb backups. Authorized testing
  confirmed that recovered credentials could authenticate directly to upstream
  SIP infrastructure. The vulnerability was discovered during response to a
  production toll-fraud incident involving multiple independent Switchvox PBX
  appliances, each using a separate carrier SIP subaccount, with
  carrier-attributed unauthorized traffic and operational disruption.

identifiers:
